  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YECAP 2024-2026</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">YECAP 2024-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to contribute to the overall goal &quot;Climate change governance is strengthened for the effective development and implementation of gender inclusive climate policies to protect young people and especially the most marginalised, while also helping them to increase the scale of their climate actions&quot;. 

To achieve this overall goal, YECAP will focus of strengthening capacity and training oung change agents (e.g., youth-led local and regional civil society organizations) and bringing young people together with decision-makers. The project also aims to raise awareness among decision-makers to systematically include and support young people in all stages of decision-making processes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Youth Empowerment for Climate Action Platform (YECAP), &#xe4;r en ungdomsledd regional plattform med syfte att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla att unga, s&#xe4;rskilt unga fr&#xe5;n marginaliserade grupper i Asien och Oceanien &#xe4;r meningsfullt engagerade och delaktiga i milj&#xf6;/klimat p&#xe5; regional, nationell och lokal niv&#xe5;. YECAP best&#xe5;r av f&#xf6;ljande akt&#xf6;rer UNDP, UNFCCC, UNICEF, British Council, YOUNGO, Movers och 2030 Youth Force. Insatsen ska genomf&#xf6;ras gemensamt av dessa akt&#xf6;rer med UNDP som avtalspart till Ambassaden och huvudsaklig ansvarig genomf&#xf6;rare.

YECAP har l&#xe4;mnat in ett f&#xf6;rslag f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra projektet &quot;Scaling up the Youth Empowerment in Climate Action Platform in Asia and the Pacific&quot;.

YECAP&#xb4;s &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att: St&#xe4;rkt klimatstyrning f&#xf6;r en effektiv utveckling och genomf&#xf6;rande av klimatpolitik som &#xe4;r genus/k&#xf6;nsinkluderande f&#xf6;r att skydda unga och s&#xe4;rskilt de mest marginaliserade, samtidigt som deras f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga till klimatengagemang &#xf6;kar.

F&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; detta &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l kommer YECAP att fokusera p&#xe5; att st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten och utbilda unga f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsakt&#xf6;rer. Projektet syftar ocks&#xe5; till att &#xf6;ka medvetenheten bland beslutsfattare om att systematiskt inkludera unga i alla stadier av beslutsprocesser relaterade till milj&#xf6; och klimatanpassning, samt att identifiera ing&#xe5;ngar f&#xf6;r unga f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsakt&#xf6;rer att p&#xe5;verka beslutsfattare.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Empowerment in Climate Action (YECAP) is a youth-led regional Platform, for young people in the Asia Pacific region to meaningfully engage in climate action. The platform is co-convened by UNDP Asia-Pacific regional office, UNFCCC Regional Collaboration Centre for Asia-Pacific and UNICEF East Asia and the Pacific and South Asia, British Council in collaboration with youth organisations/youth constituencies such as YOUNGO, Movers Programme and 2030 Youth Force. YECAP has submitted a proposal to implement the project &quot;Scaling up the Youth Empowerment in Climate Action Platform in Asia and the Pacific&quot;. The project aims to contribute to the overall goal &quot;Climate change governance is strengthened for the effective development and implementation of gender-inclusive climate policies to protect young people and especially the most marginalised, while also helping them to increase the scale of their climate actions&quot;. To achieve this overall goal, YECAP will focus on strengthening capacity and training young change agents (e.g., youth-led local and regional civil society organizations) and bringing young people together with decision-makers. The project also aims to raise awareness among decision-makers to systematically include and support young people in all stages of decision-making processes.</narrative>
  </description>
